[[!meta title="Mach"]]

Mach is a so-called first generation [[microkernel]]. Originally developed by Carnegie Mellon University (CMU) from 1985 to 1994, which was then forked and carried from 1996 onward by GNU. It is the
microkernel currently used by the [[Hurd]].

GNU Mach is mostly shipped under a BSD/MIT license, some parts are shipped under
the General Public License, either version 2, or (at your option) any later
version.
The Linux drivers part is shipped under the General Public License version 2,
but that can be disabled easily at compile time.

  * [[Concepts]]
      * [[Deficiencies]]
  * [[Documentation]]
  * [[History]]
      * [Torvalds, Tanenbaum
        Debate](http://choices.cs.illinois.edu/cache/Linus_vs_Tanenbaum.html)


